BT 1 0 0 1 0 121.65 Tm /F2 9.15 Tf 10.9 TL 3.392301 Tw (Digitized documents support administrative, educational, legal,) Tj T* 0 Tw 3.209693 Tw (scientific, cultural, and commercial information systems. They) Tj T* 0 Tw .545518 Tw (include books, archival registers, handwritten records, newspapers,) Tj T* 0 Tw .912388 Tw (forms, invoices, maps, and institutional files. The long-term value) Tj T* 0 Tw .085442 Tw (of digitization depends not only on acquiring a digital copy but also) Tj T* 0 Tw 2.606072 Tw (on preserving enough visual information for reading, indexing,) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.302851 Tw (searching, and automated analysis. Documents are often captured) Tj T* 0 Tw 2.657643 Tw (under non-uniform illumination, scanned with imperfect optics,) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.266251 Tw (copied repeatedly, compressed, or digitized after physical ageing.) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.104538 Tw (The resulting images may contain random noise, impulse defects,) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.081944 Tw (blur, periodic banding, faded strokes, stains, bleed-through, skew,) Tj T* 0 Tw (and local contrast variation.) Tj T* ET
